<title>UK: BNP sets $200 mln structured perpetual FRN.</title>
<headline>BNP sets $200 mln structured perpetual FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated</p>
<p>structured floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager CS</p>
<p>First Boston.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE NATIONALE DE PARIS</p>
<p> AMT	  $200 MLN  BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY   *PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN    *+62.5 BP  PAY DATE    20.DEC.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  99.59     FULL FEES   0.625</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A-	  REOFFER    99.59</p>
<p> NOTES     *MARGIN RISES TO 212.5 BP IF NOT CALLED AT PAR AFTER</p>
<p>		10 YEARS OR ON ANY COUPON DATE THEREAFTER.</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  FRANCE    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
